WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.490
- A viewer wrote in via email,
should they do jury duty?

00:00:03.490 --> 00:00:04.970
I think this is a great question.

00:00:04.970 --> 00:00:07.310
And the answer to that
is unequivocally, yes.

00:00:07.310 --> 00:00:09.080
Number one, not only is it your civic duty

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:11.580
to make sure that the
government doesn't overreach

00:00:11.580 --> 00:00:13.270
and that you protect everyone's rights,

00:00:13.270 --> 00:00:15.870
which in turn protects
everyone one else's rights,

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:18.180
but it's also an incredibly
fascinating experience.

00:00:18.180 --> 00:00:21.940
Every time I've done jury
duty, I am lucky to be there.

00:00:21.940 --> 00:00:24.320
And here's one secret that
you might actually not know

00:00:24.320 --> 00:00:26.980
about jury duty, which is
that in many jurisdictions,

00:00:26.980 --> 00:00:30.450
the judge is given a list
of the jurors who gets paid

00:00:30.450 --> 00:00:32.460
for their time on jury duty.

00:00:32.460 --> 00:00:34.300
And often judges bend over backwards

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.090
to make sure that people
who aren't compensated

00:00:36.090 --> 00:00:38.020
for their time on the jury are not

00:00:38.020 --> 00:00:40.960
selected because that can be a
huge hardship for the jurors.

00:00:40.960 --> 00:00:44.380
But if you are compensated for
your time by your employer,

00:00:44.380 --> 00:00:46.650
then you're more likely
to be on jury duty,

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.590
and of course it makes it more likely

00:00:48.590 --> 00:00:49.810
that you can fulfill your duties.

00:00:49.810 --> 00:00:51.530
So in answer to your question, yes,

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:52.690
you should do jury duty.

00:00:52.690 --> 00:00:54.703
So I'll see you in court.

